# paxdesign-toolbar is forbidden

**Decision (2026-08-16):** `paxdesign-toolbar` (PaxDesign Utility Dock) must **never** be added, restored, deployed, or referenced in this repository unless the user explicitly requests it in writing.

## What belongs here instead

All customer-facing functionality lives in **`paxdesign-booking`** only:

- Customer Platform (`assets/customer-auth/`)
- Live Chat + AI (`assets/js/chat-script.js`, `includes/class-paxdesign-chat*.php`)
- CCS / Cybercrime workflows (REST `pdx/v1/customer/cybercrime/*`, chat page context)
- Case status, files, attachments, and customer dashboard APIs

## Never do

- Add `paxdesign-toolbar` plugin files, ZIPs, or submodules
- Reference `window.PDXDock`, `#pdx-dock`, or `#pdx-root`
- Deploy from `C:\Users\43681\.ssh\paxdesign-toolbar`
- Install toolbar via WordPress updater, Composer, or CI
- Re-introduce toolbar as a “fallback” for Customer Platform UI

## Before every release

Run:

```bash
bash scripts/verify-no-toolbar.sh
```

## If toolbar code is needed for reference

Use git history **outside** this repo only. Do not copy toolbar PHP/JS into `paxdesign-booking`.
